<h2>Permits and code items in Highland Park</h2>
<p>The Town of Highland Park has its own building permit and inspection office, and its process is separate from the City of Dallas Development Services Department. Before roofing or structural work starts, confirm what the Town requires for your project. If repairs must be brought up to current code, those extra costs are not automatically paid by your insurer; they usually fall under ordinance or law coverage, which is often a separate, limited coverage. Our <a href="/local-building-codes/">local building codes guide</a> explains how this fits into a claim.</p>

<h2>How we help Highland Park homeowners</h2>
<p>As a Dallas Public Adjuster, we inspect the whole property, document damage with photos, measurements, and Matterport 3D imaging where useful, and prepare a detailed estimate in Xactimate. We review your policy and the insurer's estimate, identify missing scope, and handle communication with the carrier. If your claim was <a href="/services/underpaid-insurance-claims/">underpaid</a> or <a href="/services/denied-insurance-claims/">denied</a>, we can review the decision with you and discuss options such as a supplement or appraisal. We cannot promise a particular result; coverage depends on your policy and the facts.</p>
